<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net9.0</TargetFramework>
    <RollForward>Major</RollForward>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>MonoGame.GameFramework.Tools</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>mgf-tools</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- PNG decode/encode for check-palette and conform-sprite. There is no
         BCL image codec, and MonoGame's Texture2D needs a GraphicsDevice,
         which a headless CLI tool has no business creating.

         LICENCE NOTE, decided 2026-08-12: ImageSharp moved to the Six Labors
         Split License at 3.0 — Apache-2.0 for open-source/non-commercial use,
         paid otherwise. This repo is a prototype, so 4.x is fine and we take
         the actively-maintained line rather than the 2.1.x maintenance branch.
         That is why every build prints "No Six Labors license found"; the
         warning is expected, not a misconfiguration.

         IF THIS EVER SHIPS COMMERCIALLY, this is the line to revisit. Either
         buy a licence, or revert to 2.1.13 — the last Apache-2.0 release, and
         a drop-in swap because the APIs used here (Load, ProcessPixelRows,
         Resize/Box, SaveAsPng) are identical across 2.x/3.x/4.x. -->
    <PackageReference Include="SixLabors.ImageSharp" Version="4.1.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
